From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:57:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The message-navigation rail mounts in the task after the
 session's first revealed frame paints instead of in the reveal's own task,
 through the workbench's afterNextPaint, so a first visit or a return to a
 session with more than ten turns no longer builds one rail item per outline
 turn (20 on the benchmark's 1 MiB sessions, 80 on the 8 MiB ones) before its
 rows can paint, while the gutter the rail needs is still decided before that
 paint, and the line budget is the measured 107,771.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
